00:42:59.910 --> 00:43:02.320
Great software
anticipates what we

00:43:02.320 --> 00:43:06.230
want before we know
ourselves, and delights us.

00:43:06.230 --> 00:43:08.650
Users are increasingly
deciding who

00:43:08.650 --> 00:43:13.350
they'll do business with based
on how good their software is.

00:43:13.350 --> 00:43:16.360
All this creates great
opportunities for all of us

00:43:16.360 --> 00:43:20.180
in this room, really
exciting creative work.

00:43:20.180 --> 00:43:24.870
But let's talk about some of
the work that's not so exciting.

00:43:24.870 --> 00:43:27.850
Developers spend
way too much time

00:43:27.850 --> 00:43:31.350
as operators, configuring
infrastructure,

00:43:31.350 --> 00:43:35.036
making software work, rather
than making software great.

00:43:38.400 --> 00:43:40.990
Our goal is to
make it easy to run

00:43:40.990 --> 00:43:45.170
complex applications at global
scale, securely and reliably.

00:43:45.170 --> 00:43:48.900
In order to do this,
we need to automate out

00:43:48.900 --> 00:43:51.750
