the format that you need.

01:45:30.580 --> 01:45:33.230
And Data Flow is not
only this user interface,

01:45:33.230 --> 01:45:36.540
but an execution environment,
an automatically scalable,

01:45:36.540 --> 01:45:39.600
distributed cluster
of computers doing

01:45:39.600 --> 01:45:41.870
the work of
transforming that data

01:45:41.870 --> 01:45:44.470
and loading it into
your system of choice.

01:45:44.470 --> 01:45:48.720
It does that using the ParDo,
or parallel execution model that

01:45:48.720 --> 01:45:51.880
makes it super, super
easy to write that code.

01:45:51.880 --> 01:45:55.200
If you've ever done this kind
of work in SPARC or in Presto,

01:45:55.200 --> 01:45:57.740
you're looking at
this much code.

01:45:57.740 --> 01:46:00.800
And if you do it in a
ParDo, in Data Flow,

01:46:00.800 --> 01:46:02.910
it's about this much code.

01:46:02.910 --> 01:46:03.640
I promise.

01:46:03.640 --> 01:46:07.090
So once you've transformed
and loaded that data

01:46:07.090 --> 01:46:09.860
