You just start
hooking to our APIs.

01:52:14.830 --> 01:52:16.680
You want to be able
to translate text,

01:52:16.680 --> 01:52:18.124
we have the translate API.

01:52:18.124 --> 01:52:20.290
You want to understand
what's available in pictures,

01:52:20.290 --> 01:52:22.270
you use the Vision API.

01:52:22.270 --> 01:52:24.690
You want to be able to
process the things that I

01:52:24.690 --> 01:52:28.099
say into text, that's
the Speech API.

01:52:28.099 --> 01:52:30.140
You want to be able to
understand the information

01:52:30.140 --> 01:52:31.810
inside of that text.

01:52:31.810 --> 01:52:34.520
That's the Natural
Language Processing API.

01:52:34.520 --> 01:52:37.740
Each of these tools, I mean,
imagine the combination of them

01:52:37.740 --> 01:52:38.560
in concert.

01:52:38.560 --> 01:52:39.990
Take Google Photos.

01:52:39.990 --> 01:52:41.784
If I pull my phone
out and I say--

01:52:41.784 --> 01:52:43.950
this will probably mess up
a lot of people's phones.

01:52:43.950 --> 01:52:48.750
I say, OK, Google, find me
pictures of kids in a boat.

01:52:48.750 --> 01:52:50.680
I hear phones
doing it right now.

01:52:50.680 --> 01:52:51.470
[LAUGHS]

01:52:51.470 --> 01:52:52.750
Right?

01:52:52.750 --> 01:52:54.090
Think about what happens.

01:52:54.090 --> 01:52:56.390
I said the word
"kids in a boat."

01:52:56.390 --> 01:53:00.310
It has to can use the Speech
API to convert that to text,

01:53:00.310 --> 01:53:03.760
extract that kids and
boats are real things,

01:53:03.760 --> 01:53:07.030
identify those things in
all of my tens of thousands

01:53:07.030 --> 01:53:10.580
of pictures, and then retrieve
those pictures to show me.

01:53:10.580 --> 01:53:14.620
It can do all of that in
hundreds of milliseconds.

01:53:14.620 --> 01:53:19.220
In production, at scale,
for billions of users,

01:53:19.220 --> 01:53:21.300
Google is doing this today.

01:53:21.300 --> 01:53:25.420
And your businesses all already
have access to these APIs.

01:53:25.420 --> 01:53:29.240
You can build that magic
into your applications

01:53:29.240 --> 01:53:32.200
without having to understand
all of the complexity

01:53:32.200 --> 01:53:34.410
of the foundational Machine
Learning technology.

01:53:34.410 --> 01:53:36.120
You just get to use.

01:53:36.120 --> 01:53:40.050
But we know that's actually
just the first step.

01:53:40.050 --> 01:53:42.209
The first step will be
applying these technologies

01:53:42.209 --> 01:53:44.250
and new models as we come
up with them over time.

01:53:44.250 --> 01:53:47.260
We're actually building
more as we speak.

01:53:47.260 --> 01:53:50.700
We expect that this kind of
rich data where you get access

01:53:50.700 --> 01:53:55.060
to what is inside of the
analog information you have,

01:53:55.060 --> 01:53:57.580
right, a picture is
just a series of pixels

01:53:57.580 --> 01:54:00.039
until you can say these are--
oh, there's pictures of cats.

01:54:00.039 --> 01:54:00.788
Or there's people.

01:54:00.788 --> 01:54:02.000
Or that's where faces are.

01:54:02.000 --> 01:54:03.940
Or that's the logo
of my company.

01:54:03.940 --> 01:54:05.650
Or that person's naked.

01:54:05.650 --> 01:54:08.350
Or all these kind of
information that you

01:54:08.350 --> 01:54:13.460
can get out of the data
that you already have.

01:54:13.460 --> 01:54:15.070
So as we add this
kind of richness

01:54:15.070 --> 01:54:16.869
to even more types
of data, we think

01:54:16.869 --> 01:54:18.660
you'll be able to get
quite a bit of value.

01:54:18.660 --> 01:54:21.220
But we also think it will
allow you to be very creative.

01:54:21.220 --> 01:54:24.160
We're watching incredible
experimentation, people

01:54:24.160 --> 01:54:27.080
building art, and
music, and poetry

01:54:27.080 --> 01:54:28.310
on top of Machine Learning.

01:54:28.310 --> 01:54:34.070
It's really a new Wild West of
innovative and creative ideas.

01:54:34.070 --> 01:54:36.610
And so we know you'll want
to build your own models.

01:54:36.610 --> 01:54:39.111
And Google has some very
real innovation here, too.

01:54:39.111 --> 01:54:39.610
Right?

01:54:39.610 --> 01:54:42.320
We're not just interested
in Machine Learning

01:54:42.320 --> 01:54:43.810
kind of, sort of.

01:54:43.810 --> 01:54:47.480
We know that this is a huge part
of our business going forward.

01:54:47.480 --> 01:54:51.740
So we don't run Machine Learning
models on our computers,

01:54:51.740 --> 01:54:54.120
because that's 2012.

01:54:54.120 --> 01:54:57.160
We don't even run it on
GPUs because that's 2014.

01:54:57.160 --> 01:55:00.370
GPUs are nice, but we've
built our own custom

01:55:00.370 --> 01:55:03.600
ASICs, our own hardware,
just for Machine Learning

01:55:03.600 --> 01:55:04.330
processing.

01:55:04.330 --> 01:55:06.350
It's called a Tensor
Processing Unit.

01:55:06.350 --> 01:55:08.820
It's a part that
no one else has.

01:55:08.820 --> 01:55:11.020
We built them from
scratch for ourselves.

01:55:11.020 --> 01:55:12.790
And they are in
production today.

01:55:12.790 --> 01:55:15.820
We have custom silicon
just for doing this work.

01:55:15.820 --> 01:55:19.090
And to get access to that
infrastructure horsepower,

01:55:19.090 --> 01:55:22.110
we've started to build
a Machine Learning API,

01:55:22.110 --> 01:55:24.890
a system that will take the open
source system that we built,

01:55:24.890 --> 01:55:27.540
called TensorFlow -- that's
the number one machine learning

01:55:27.540 --> 01:55:30.030
library in the
world, by the way--

01:55:30.030 --> 01:55:32.370
take TensorFlow code
that you build anywhere.

01:55:32.370 --> 01:55:34.150
You build on your Raspberry Pi.

01:55:34.150 --> 01:55:35.270
You build on your phone.

01:55:35.270 --> 01:55:36.330
You build on your laptop.

01:55:36.330 --> 01:55:37.788
You build on somebody
else's cloud.

01:55:37.788 --> 01:55:39.600
You build on our cloud.

01:55:39.600 --> 01:55:41.570
And if you want to
run that in production

01:55:41.570 --> 01:55:44.890
at scale for billions
of users, you

01:55:44.890 --> 01:55:46.950
can use the Machine
Learning API to access

01:55:46.950 --> 01:55:50.430
Google's unique hardware
for accelerated execution

01:55:50.430 --> 01:55:52.460
and simplified development.

01:55:52.460 --> 01:55:53.460
That's in alpha today.

01:55:53.460 --> 01:55:55.280
We'll be moving
to beta very soon.

01:55:55.280 --> 01:55:57.201
We know that's
exciting technology

01:55:57.201 --> 01:55:58.450
for the folks in the audience.

01:55:58.450 --> 01:56:00.460
And we're excited to
